  "notes": "Aladin Lite v3 sky atlas. The deep-space survey image fills the whole viewport, with the UI floating over it as light-grey (#ececec) monospace boxes that have 2px dark borders and 3px radii. The active rail button gets a green border. Catalog markers are colour- and shape-coded per layer (red circles = SIMBAD, green diamonds = YSO candidates, orange squares = Gaia, yellow dots = notes). Instrument footprints are drawn as lime/green, violet and orange polygons. A magenta reticle marks the centre, and the coordinates in the search box are magenta too. Two proposals were filed: a new 'layer-stack-panel' entry, and new-values for map-explorer (sky-survey-imagery basemap, footprint-polygons overlay)."
